  "description": "A strip of metal carrying a current, in your solenoid's field (B along the strip's length, out of the board when positive; the yellow coil, top right). The field pushes the moving electrons sideways (the Lorentz force) until the charge they pile on one side holds the rest back: a voltage across the strip, the Hall voltage, $V_H \\approx I B/(n q)$ (per unit length). The two contacts on the strip's sides read it, floating: no current flows through them. Make a current between 2.7 and 3.5 flow into the right end and the top contact sit between 1.0 and 1.9 below the bottom one (averaged over $t = 10$ to $80$). Which way must the field point? Electrons are negative.",
